author=trentini
description=Craft The Catalogue from a notebook and any pen or pencil, then use it to buy and sell items for cash. Every vanilla item is priced individually; items added by other mods are priced by the same rules and can be filtered by source mod. NOTE: with many item mods installed, the first time you open the Buy window in a session takes a few seconds while every modded item is priced. It is instant afterwards. Buying deducts real Money and MoneyBundles; selling pays 30 percent of value by default, scaled by condition, adjustable in the sandbox options, and never destroys what it will not pay for. Right-click any cash machine to open a bank account: deposit and withdraw real notes with a PIN-protected credit card in your character name, so a fortune stops weighing fifty kilos. Every credit card in the world belongs to somebody, with a balance and a PIN you have to work out -- from a note in the wallet, a pencil impression on the plastic, a home-made card reader, or a crowbar. Burn the catalogue onto a CD and install it in a computer to shop against your bank balance, or clone a wrecked ATM to run internet banking from a desk. All of it can be switched off in the sandbox options. SINGLE-PLAYER: every transaction is worked out on your own machine, so on a dedicated server the prices and the payments can be tampered with. Server authority is planned for after 1.0.
